From d30bd03f4f6d6b58f0ec3fa14d3fcbd207f6fca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:51:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): saving my input after an event conflict keeps
 others' changes and asks about clashes (D-94)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Save mine again" on the 409 notice sent the whole input captured when
the save failed, so fields I never touched reverted someone else's
change, and anything typed after the notice appeared was dropped. It now
submits the form as it is (EventForm's own checks run) and merges onto
the latest event: units I did not edit take the server value, units only
I changed take mine. Kind, title, description and one "when" unit (all
day, dates, instants compared by value, time zone) are merged. Units
both sides changed to different values are listed with both values and
saved only after "overwrite"; cancel sends nothing and focus returns to
the button. The save goes out at the latest version, a repeated 409
shows the newer event and keeps the input, and a failure keeps it too.

Test: event-save-mine (component) and event-conflict-merge (unit). On
dbd1861 the first case sent title "회의" and 01:00Z instead of the
latest "새 제목" and 05:00Z.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
